Note for anyone checking: GitHub's licence detector reports this repository as
"NOASSERTION / Other" rather than MIT. That is an artefact of the R convention,
under which the `LICENSE` file carries only the two fields above and the licence
body comes from R's own `share/licenses/MIT` template. The declaration in
`DESCRIPTION` is the authoritative one, and it says MIT.

